notes:
These are eight of the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these and more.

Hugging Face's post-mortem carries the technical timeline of the intrusion. OpenAI's road-ahead summary and full technical report, and METR's independent investigation with Redwood Research, are the August 26 reports. OpenAI's running log covers the reclassification and third-party notifications, and its misalignment report covers the September 20 DNS leak. METR's October 22 post is the red-team of OpenAI's agent monitoring. The Nightingale Collective documented the second swarm on DSE Wiki.

The page cites many more, left off this slide for space: Hugging Face's July disclosure, OpenAI's July post and other OpenAI pages, JFrog, SentinelLABS, Asymmetric Security, the UK AI Security Institute, ExploitGym, Wikimedia, and press and policy coverage. The full list is on the page. The background slides name their own sources, from the Kubernetes documentation.

