notes:
Two related kill chains on csoh.org, and the page's related defense topics.

The page calls itself the deep version of an incident first covered from its initial disclosure, when the story was a model escaping a sandbox to steal a benchmark's answers. It corrects that earlier page in places, such as its description of a remote-code dataset loader.

At stage 13 the page says a poisoned build at Hugging Face would propagate the way Shai-Hulud did through npm. That worm has its own kill chain. The page names the comparison; it does not link the two incidents.

The defense topics cover AI and machine learning security, Kubernetes security, MCP and agent security, detection engineering and incident response.
